 "_about": "Subject taxonomy for grants_all.tags. Each tag is applied when (a) any keyword pattern matches the upper-cased text 'PURPOSE | RECIPIENT NAME' on word boundaries, or (b) the recipient NTEE code (from the IRS Business Master File) starts with one of ntee_prefixes. Keywords are regular-expression fragments (RE2 syntax), written in upper case. Phrases listed under 'exclude' are blanked out of the text before that tag's keywords are tested. A grant can carry several tags. Edit this file, then run: python3 consolidate.py tags export_grants. This is keyword matching, not human coding: expect false positives and misses. Note for the published copy: 4 organization-name patterns that were used when the tags were built are not listed here, so re-applying this file changes a small number of tags.",
